WEBVTT

00:01:43.080 --> 00:01:45.330
<b>Night School</b>

00:01:54.260 --> 00:01:58.390
I know it's sudden, but allow me 
to introduce our transfer student,

00:01:59.180 --> 00:02:05.140
Franken Yasohachi

00:01:59.600 --> 00:02:02.100
Franken Yasohachi-kun.

00:02:02.100 --> 00:02:04.690
Play nice, everyone.

00:02:10.770 --> 00:02:29.750
<b>Okada</b>

00:02:10.850 --> 00:02:12.710
Who is this guy?

00:02:12.690 --> 00:02:29.750
<b>Kanbara</b>

00:02:12.710 --> 00:02:14.150
Wow.

00:02:14.110 --> 00:02:29.750
<b>Horita</b>

00:02:14.150 --> 00:02:16.200
Yeah. I'm kind of impressed.

00:02:16.200 --> 00:02:19.950
You don't often get to see 
guys who look like this.

00:02:19.950 --> 00:02:21.910
I bet he'd look great in a cosplay.

00:02:21.910 --> 00:02:24.660
How can you dress him up to 
look even more like a cosplay?

00:02:24.660 --> 00:02:27.970
<i>She's right. He's already got what's 
almost a perfect Frankenstein look.</i>

00:02:29.990 --> 00:02:33.900
Yasohachi-kun, you'll sit in the very back.

00:02:42.110 --> 00:02:45.410
Did he pass out because he was so nervous?

00:02:45.410 --> 00:02:49.250
For such a big guy, he's quite the coward.

00:02:58.290 --> 00:03:00.430
He just ran out of power.

00:03:00.430 --> 00:03:01.600
Power?

00:03:02.720 --> 00:03:05.310
Which means...

00:03:05.310 --> 00:03:06.750
He's a robot.

00:03:06.750 --> 00:03:10.200
No, he's quite close to human.

00:03:10.200 --> 00:03:12.440
But he's not human.

00:03:12.290 --> 00:03:15.250
<b>Okada</b>

00:03:12.440 --> 00:03:15.060
Mai-chan, how do you know that?

00:03:15.630 --> 00:03:19.540
I only just now remembered...

00:03:20.370 --> 00:03:24.210
...but I believe he's my fiancé.

00:03:24.460 --> 00:03:26.470
What?!

00:03:26.470 --> 00:03:28.980
Who forgets that?

00:03:28.980 --> 00:03:32.650
I didn't notice since he's 
been improved here and there.

00:03:35.810 --> 00:03:38.370
But this warped look in his eyes...

00:03:38.760 --> 00:03:40.950
I'm almost certain it's him.

00:03:40.950 --> 00:03:44.130
Not human, huh?

00:03:44.130 --> 00:03:48.540
Then it's time for our transfer 
student's medical examination.

00:03:51.280 --> 00:03:54.280
Take him to the infirmary.

00:03:59.010 --> 00:04:03.090
Doctor, should you be 
drawing that much blood?

00:04:03.090 --> 00:04:06.170
Yeah. He may be a big man, but...

00:04:06.170 --> 00:04:08.060
Don't worry.

00:04:08.480 --> 00:04:10.940
He's already dead.

00:04:10.940 --> 00:04:13.460
What?

00:04:13.460 --> 00:04:14.990
What do you mean?

00:04:15.310 --> 00:04:19.260
I mean he's no longer a living human.

00:04:18.730 --> 00:04:21.280
<b>Plate</b>

00:04:19.620 --> 00:04:24.410
Medically speaking, he's a corpse that's 
been dead for over a hundred years.

00:04:24.410 --> 00:04:25.830
What?!

00:04:25.830 --> 00:04:28.900
Which means he's a giant zombie?

00:04:30.940 --> 00:04:33.090
Quit reacting to everything we say!

00:04:33.450 --> 00:04:36.580
But he's a zombie...

00:04:36.580 --> 00:04:38.250
Not a zombie.

00:04:38.600 --> 00:04:43.750
He's an externally powered golem.

00:04:39.500 --> 00:04:43.760
<b>Externally Powered Golem</b>

00:04:43.750 --> 00:04:49.000
I've identified at least 
20 different types of DNA.

00:04:49.610 --> 00:04:56.250
Which means he's composed of 
a whole platoon of humans.

00:04:56.250 --> 00:04:59.690
The left and right lobes of his 
brain came from different people.

00:04:59.690 --> 00:05:04.390
I'm not even sure his cerebellum 
and brain stem came from mammals.

00:05:04.830 --> 00:05:07.650
In other words, he's a monster.

00:05:07.650 --> 00:05:09.620
A monster?!

00:05:10.560 --> 00:05:13.480
Why did he transfer to our school?

00:05:13.480 --> 00:05:17.600
More importantly, why is 
that monster Mai's fiancé?

00:05:18.190 --> 00:05:20.880
Mai, there's an explanation for this, right?

00:05:20.880 --> 00:05:23.880
Yes, but it's a long story.

00:05:23.880 --> 00:05:26.370
If I abridge the story 
and skip the details...

00:05:26.370 --> 00:05:29.300
No! Don't abridge or skip anything!

00:05:29.300 --> 00:05:32.920
Tell me everything there 
is to know about it!

00:05:34.510 --> 00:05:40.830
Very well. In that case, I 
shall tell you everything.

00:05:46.110 --> 00:05:51.050
A long, long time ago, 
when I was still young,

00:05:51.050 --> 00:05:54.860
I was relaxing on vacation 
one sunny spring afternoon.

00:05:55.080 --> 00:05:56.940
You little shit!

00:05:56.940 --> 00:05:59.110
Why won't you listen to anything I say?

00:05:59.110 --> 00:06:00.850
Wait, time out.

00:06:00.850 --> 00:06:07.170
Would that stepmother be Rebeus, 
your father's 48th wife?

00:06:07.170 --> 00:06:13.160
No, at that time he was married to his 21st 
wife, a horrible woman named Claudia.

00:06:13.460 --> 00:06:16.840
Who are you calling 
horrible, you ugly bitch?

00:06:16.840 --> 00:06:19.150
Who taught you those vulgar words?

00:06:19.150 --> 00:06:23.300
Shut up! There isn't a woman in 
this world more vulgar than you!

00:06:23.300 --> 00:06:25.100
Now, now, you two.

00:06:25.100 --> 00:06:28.160
Why don't you clean this mess up together?

00:06:28.160 --> 00:06:30.290
How dare you act like a bystander?

00:06:30.290 --> 00:06:34.120
She grew into an impudent 
child despite her size

00:06:34.120 --> 00:06:37.240
because you and your previous 
wives didn't raise her properly.

00:06:37.240 --> 00:06:40.330
Mai's actually a kind girl at heart.

00:06:40.330 --> 00:06:41.860
You understand that, don't you?

00:06:41.860 --> 00:06:45.300
Okay, okay. I get it. I'm going 
shopping for Hermes bags.

00:06:45.300 --> 00:06:47.570
Oh, you're hopeless!

00:06:47.930 --> 00:06:52.470
Eventually I ran out of patience 
with my father's constant ogling.

00:06:53.080 --> 00:06:57.920
My heart had been deeply wounded, 
so in order to mend my heart,

00:06:57.920 --> 00:07:02.200
I courageously ran off into 
the wilderness all by myself.

00:07:04.200 --> 00:07:06.940
Kill her, don't kill her.

00:07:07.320 --> 00:07:09.790
Kill her, don't kill her.

00:07:10.740 --> 00:07:11.780
<b>No Bolt</b>

00:07:16.370 --> 00:07:18.740
Oh, my. What a funny face.

00:07:18.740 --> 00:07:21.120
I haven't laughed this hard in a while.

00:07:21.120 --> 00:07:22.880
Thanks. You can have this.

00:07:25.370 --> 00:07:30.690
And that's how we became engaged.

00:07:35.270 --> 00:07:37.060
Uh, Mai?

00:07:37.400 --> 00:07:40.460
I don't understand how 
that's what happened next.

00:07:42.530 --> 00:07:47.950
In vampire society, the act of giving a 
person a flower is a marriage proposal.

00:07:47.950 --> 00:07:49.510
I see.

00:07:49.510 --> 00:07:52.370
Wait, this is no time to be impressed!

00:07:52.370 --> 00:07:56.250
But speaking of a vampire's 
forbidden love...

00:07:56.250 --> 00:08:00.370
That's widely considered to be 
their eternal rivals, werewolves.

00:08:00.370 --> 00:08:03.580
I'm amazed your parents gave you their 
blessing to marry this monster.

00:08:03.580 --> 00:08:07.190
They probably would've approved 
of anyone willing to marry her.

00:08:07.190 --> 00:08:11.080
That's right. Some parents are okay with 
any partner, as long as they're human.

00:08:11.080 --> 00:08:13.770
It's not even clear if he's 
actually human, though.

00:08:13.760 --> 00:08:31.030
Hey, Boss!

00:08:13.760 --> 00:08:31.030
Congratulations
on Your Wedding!!

00:08:14.180 --> 00:08:17.900
From my stepmother's perspective, it meant 
the removal of a source of her troubles,

00:08:17.900 --> 00:08:24.520
and my father probably thought a golem 
was better than me marrying a werewolf.

00:08:24.520 --> 00:08:26.580
<i>Even I can accept that.</i>

00:08:26.990 --> 00:08:30.750
<i>Anyway, I can't believe Mai had a fiancé.</i>

00:08:31.030 --> 00:08:33.190
I won't allow it!

00:08:33.190 --> 00:08:35.270
I'll never allow it!

00:08:35.270 --> 00:08:39.010
Of all people, why does Mai-chan 
have to be engaged to this oddity?

00:08:39.010 --> 00:08:40.860
You're pretty odd yourself.

00:08:40.860 --> 00:08:45.290
He gets to do whatever he wants 
to her, whenever he pleases!

00:08:45.290 --> 00:08:46.960
So jealous!

00:08:51.450 --> 00:08:54.460
What are you fantasizing about, you brute?

00:08:54.760 --> 00:09:00.430
While you guys were chewing the fat, 
I think I did a pretty good job over here.

00:09:00.430 --> 00:09:03.280
What? Doctor, did you do something again?

00:09:07.960 --> 00:09:12.670
I feel like his groans have powered up.

00:09:12.670 --> 00:09:16.290
I did what's expected of me 
as a public health doctor.

00:09:16.290 --> 00:09:21.030
In his existing state, his capacity for 
self-propulsion was rather limited.

00:09:21.030 --> 00:09:25.420
I added an additional internal 
battery and buffer.

00:09:25.420 --> 00:09:29.920
Now he can move for three minutes 
after three hours of charging.

00:09:29.920 --> 00:09:31.650
Just three minutes?

00:09:31.650 --> 00:09:35.150
More than that requires 
an external power source.

00:09:38.130 --> 00:09:39.830
Shut up!

00:09:39.830 --> 00:09:42.960
You don't get to complain!

00:09:43.220 --> 00:09:55.860
<b>Celebrating Franken Yasohachi's Transfer</b>

00:09:43.830 --> 00:09:49.300
<i>And so, with a group photo taken by Maki,</i>

00:09:49.300 --> 00:09:52.090
<i>who wasn't too proud to use her camera timer,</i>

00:09:52.090 --> 00:09:55.620
<i>Franken Yasohachi was 
recognized as our classmate.</i>

00:09:56.090 --> 00:10:00.660
<i>At the time, none of us mortals 
imagined that this large</i>

00:10:00.660 --> 00:10:04.830
<i>but useless creature possessed 
an incredible power.</i>

00:10:05.190 --> 00:10:09.370
<i>As long as Franken was charged, 
he was unstoppable.</i>

00:10:08.040 --> 00:10:10.380
<b>Unstoppable</b>

00:10:11.040 --> 00:10:15.330
<i>His lower body was apparently 
assembled from human athletes.</i>

00:10:15.330 --> 00:10:18.130
<i>He could run 100 meters in 8.5 seconds.</i>

00:10:20.650 --> 00:10:23.870
<i>His running long jump easily 
cleared ten meters,</i>

00:10:24.600 --> 00:10:29.820
<i>and on the triple jump he set 
a menacing 30-meter record.</i>

00:10:30.030 --> 00:10:31.790
<i>If he had been a living human,</i>

00:10:31.790 --> 00:10:36.060
<i>he would've won five gold metals 
in Olympic track and field events.</i>

00:10:36.060 --> 00:10:40.530
<i>And his upper body was assembled 
from several wrestlers.</i>

00:10:41.690 --> 00:10:46.430
<i>Furthermore, his brain was comprised 
from a collection of several geniuses.</i>

00:10:46.830 --> 00:10:50.830
<i>On any instrument he touched he could 
play Mozart, Chopin, or Sarasate.</i>

00:10:51.460 --> 00:10:53.770
<i>He knew everything that was to 
know on the theory of relativity,</i>

00:10:53.770 --> 00:10:55.860
<i>quantum mechanics, string theory.</i>

00:10:56.500 --> 00:11:01.100
<i>His reflexes allowed him to quickly beat 
the newest version of Super Mario.</i>

00:11:03.870 --> 00:11:08.000
<i>Despite lacking a license, 
his driving skills were exceptional,</i>

00:11:08.000 --> 00:11:10.870
<i>even greater than the Demon 
of the Pass or Initial D.</i>

00:11:14.530 --> 00:11:18.120
But there was a problem...

00:11:18.850 --> 00:11:23.860
Since he has a complete digestive tract, 
he surely eats and drinks like a normal person.

00:11:24.070 --> 00:11:26.070
He's powered by electricity,

00:11:26.070 --> 00:11:29.770
so biologically speaking, 
it's a meaningless act of consumption.

00:11:29.770 --> 00:11:34.580
It's similar to how Mai likes pot stickers 
despite subsisting on only blood.

00:11:34.580 --> 00:11:37.340
Extra garlic, please.

00:11:37.340 --> 00:11:39.490
Who said I was ordering 
any food for delivery?

00:11:40.190 --> 00:11:45.580
By the way, his genitals include 
some non-standard parts.

00:11:45.860 --> 00:11:46.640
Look.

00:11:46.640 --> 00:11:48.430
What?!

00:11:50.530 --> 00:11:55.530
Because this image is R-rated, 
I can't show it to minors.

00:11:55.530 --> 00:11:59.950
But I'm certain its 
composition is exceptional.

00:12:09.200 --> 00:12:10.200
<b>Self-censored</b>

00:12:10.200 --> 00:12:11.080
<b>Self-censored</b>

00:12:13.720 --> 00:12:16.420
He looks like a healthy young man to me.

00:12:16.420 --> 00:12:19.270
I'd be terrified if he 
forced himself onto me.

00:12:19.270 --> 00:12:22.060
I doubt he'd be interested in you.

00:12:22.060 --> 00:12:25.710
Ugh. Another annoying man to deal with.

00:12:25.710 --> 00:12:28.160
Men truly are the worst.

00:12:28.160 --> 00:12:32.020
If it comes down to it, 
you can just unplug him.

00:12:32.020 --> 00:12:35.320
He's extremely safe.

00:12:35.570 --> 00:12:38.770
You're kidding! He's extremely dangerous!

00:12:38.770 --> 00:12:42.110
Shut up! Unplug that thing immediately!

00:12:42.110 --> 00:12:45.480
While you're at it, castrate him, too!

00:12:47.280 --> 00:12:51.180
He's way better than you uncontrollable lot.

00:12:51.180 --> 00:12:55.800
He may be a monster, but now that he's your 
classmate, try to get along with him.

00:12:55.800 --> 00:12:59.280
Then why not at least draw some 
more blood to calm him down?

00:12:59.280 --> 00:13:01.920
Don't you need more blood samples?

00:13:01.920 --> 00:13:04.500
I'm not interested in the blood of corpses.

00:13:04.500 --> 00:13:06.980
You can be so stubborn.

00:13:06.980 --> 00:13:11.320
You're the one asking us to 
play nice with a corpse.

00:13:11.880 --> 00:13:15.920
By the way, where did he come 
from? Where will he go?

00:13:15.920 --> 00:13:21.170
According to his transfer form, 
his home address, postal code,

00:13:15.940 --> 00:13:26.570
<b>Student Transfer Form</b>

00:13:15.940 --> 00:13:26.570
<b>Name:</b>

00:13:15.940 --> 00:13:26.570
Franken Yasohachi

00:13:15.940 --> 00:13:26.570
<b>yr</b>

00:13:15.940 --> 00:13:26.570
<b>Class</b>

00:13:15.940 --> 00:13:26.570
<b>Male</b>

00:13:15.940 --> 00:13:26.570
<b>Date of Birth:</b>

00:13:15.940 --> 00:13:26.570
Unknown

00:13:15.940 --> 00:13:26.570
<b>Residence:</b>

00:13:15.940 --> 00:13:26.570
Unknown

00:13:15.940 --> 00:13:26.570
<b>Guardian:</b>

00:13:15.940 --> 00:13:26.570
Unknown

00:13:15.940 --> 00:13:26.570
Unknown

00:13:15.940 --> 00:13:26.570
<b>Date of Transfer:</b>

00:13:15.940 --> 00:13:26.570
<b>Transferring To:</b>

00:13:15.940 --> 00:13:26.570
Unknown

00:13:15.940 --> 00:13:26.570
<b>Date of Transfer:</b>

00:13:15.940 --> 00:13:26.570
<b>Transferring From:</b>

00:13:15.940 --> 00:13:26.570
Unknown

00:13:21.170 --> 00:13:26.720
phone number, email address, 
and guardians are all unknown.

00:13:26.720 --> 00:13:30.990
Just so you know, I'm not 
letting him live at my house.

00:13:30.990 --> 00:13:33.620
But he's Mai-chan's fiancé.

00:13:33.620 --> 00:13:35.770
I don't care if he's her 
fiancé or a pickled fish!

00:13:35.770 --> 00:13:38.130
I'm not interested in living with a corpse!

00:13:38.130 --> 00:13:40.440
Mai-chan, are you okay with that?

00:13:40.440 --> 00:13:43.010
My parents arranged my engagement for me.

00:13:44.170 --> 00:13:45.490
You heard her.

00:13:49.110 --> 00:13:52.640
<i>And so, we decided to keep 
him unplugged inside a locker</i>

00:13:52.640 --> 00:13:55.730
<i>in the school infirmary 
outside of school hours.</i>

00:13:56.450 --> 00:14:00.740
<i>He was treated worse than a Roomba.</i>

00:14:03.240 --> 00:14:07.650
<i>And then, that fateful night arrived.</i>

00:14:17.410 --> 00:14:19.380
<b>School Infirmary</b>

00:14:17.410 --> 00:14:19.380
<b>Night School</b>

00:14:35.470 --> 00:14:39.140
I'm glad today was another quiet day.

00:14:39.140 --> 00:14:42.640
Maybe happiness is an uneventful life.

00:14:43.420 --> 00:14:47.750
Hey, Mai. Don't you think we 
resemble a married couple?

00:14:47.750 --> 00:14:51.410
A married couple? What do you mean?

00:14:51.660 --> 00:14:54.540
Uh, nothing.

00:15:00.290 --> 00:15:03.630
<b>Franken 88
AV Plus/Berserker Mode</b>

00:15:08.270 --> 00:15:12.540
Hey, Mai. You'll catch a cold if you 
don't sleep inside your closet.

00:15:18.100 --> 00:15:20.350
But I'm lonely by myself.

00:15:20.350 --> 00:15:23.320
What? But...

00:15:23.320 --> 00:15:24.480
Daddy...

00:15:24.930 --> 00:15:25.860
Daddy?

00:15:26.450 --> 00:15:28.900
Oh, she's just half-asleep.

00:15:31.090 --> 00:15:33.570
Okay, okay. Daddy's here.

00:15:33.570 --> 00:15:36.750
Now let's get you changed 
so you can go to bed.

00:15:37.240 --> 00:15:38.610
Okay.

00:15:43.120 --> 00:15:44.540
Mai.

00:15:49.390 --> 00:15:50.720
Daddy...

00:15:51.530 --> 00:15:54.130
I can't get this button undone.

00:15:54.130 --> 00:15:56.380
You're hopeless.

00:16:10.180 --> 00:16:12.540
Franken...

00:16:13.800 --> 00:16:14.810
Daddy?

00:16:22.420 --> 00:16:25.630
Love... Mai...

00:16:31.050 --> 00:16:33.010
<b>Self-censored</b>

00:16:35.480 --> 00:16:38.070
This isn't good. Let's run for it, Mai.

00:16:38.070 --> 00:16:38.980
Okay.

00:16:51.400 --> 00:16:53.360
<b>Self-censored</b>

00:16:55.660 --> 00:16:58.870
<b>Franken 88
AV Plus/Hulk Mode</b>

00:17:19.560 --> 00:17:21.680
He's huge.

00:17:21.680 --> 00:17:23.560
He's Franken Hulk now.

00:17:26.080 --> 00:17:28.390
Mai.

00:17:34.290 --> 00:17:36.190
This looks like a job for the security team.

00:17:36.190 --> 00:17:38.570
I can't miss this opportunity.

00:17:38.570 --> 00:17:40.980
So, what are we going to 
do about that monster?

00:17:40.980 --> 00:17:43.360
We'll call in some Okinawan 
guardian lions or something.

00:17:44.140 --> 00:17:45.880
Wow!

00:17:44.200 --> 00:17:48.460
<b>The Trio</b>

00:17:45.830 --> 00:17:48.460
<b>Katsuno</b>

00:17:46.530 --> 00:17:48.590
It truly is <i>Beauty and the Beast</i>.

00:17:48.590 --> 00:17:50.910
No, more like <i>The War of the Gargantuas</i>.

00:17:50.910 --> 00:17:54.920
Or rather, <i>Frankenstein Conquers the World</i>.

00:18:01.330 --> 00:18:03.620
I'll persuade Franken to stop.

00:18:04.110 --> 00:18:06.570
After all, he's looking for me.

00:18:06.570 --> 00:18:08.300
You can't do that.

00:18:08.300 --> 00:18:11.900
I won't hand you over to that monster.

00:18:12.600 --> 00:18:17.050
<i>The monster is approaching 
the building we're inside.</i>

00:18:18.460 --> 00:18:21.030
<i>Goodbye, everyone!</i>

00:18:23.410 --> 00:18:25.490
Who's calling?

00:18:25.490 --> 00:18:28.950
<i>Doctor, you unplugged him, right?</i>

00:18:28.950 --> 00:18:32.570
Is that something you should be asking 
your teacher in the middle of the night?

00:18:32.570 --> 00:18:34.960
<i>Are you still half-asleep?</i>

00:18:34.960 --> 00:18:38.720
Franken has grown huge and 
is destroying the city!

00:18:38.720 --> 00:18:41.290
If we don't do something soon, 
something terrible could happen!

00:18:41.460 --> 00:18:44.150
Something terrible already is happening.

00:18:44.150 --> 00:18:45.970
Perhaps we could...

00:18:46.520 --> 00:18:49.170
<i>use that bolt on top of his head.</i>

00:18:49.170 --> 00:18:52.200
<i>I thought it was just for decoration,</i>

00:18:52.580 --> 00:18:56.790
<i>but it might be an emergency power supply.</i>

00:18:57.120 --> 00:19:00.210
It's like a lightning rod?

00:19:01.010 --> 00:19:07.160
<i>That bolt allowed him to charge himself 
using lightning and activate himself.</i>

00:19:07.830 --> 00:19:10.460
<i>The problem is his brain.</i>

00:19:10.460 --> 00:19:11.690
<i>His brain?</i>

00:19:11.690 --> 00:19:17.420
Golems are typically made using the 
bodies of criminals sentenced to death.

00:19:17.420 --> 00:19:23.860
Genius or not, he's made up of a 
collection of dangerous criminals.

00:19:23.860 --> 00:19:26.240
Which means...

00:19:26.240 --> 00:19:32.860
In his current state, his destructive body 
and wicked brain make him a literal monster.

00:19:33.180 --> 00:19:37.640
Spare me the analysis and 
do something about him!

00:19:37.640 --> 00:19:41.580
<i>Should we feed Mai the Salamander's 
blood and have her fight him?</i>

00:19:42.130 --> 00:19:45.690
<i>Otherwise we'll have to call 
in the SDF's Maser Cannon.</i>

00:19:46.540 --> 00:19:52.000
Either way, it's more than a single 
public health doctor can handle.

00:19:52.470 --> 00:19:54.340
I'm going to sleep.

00:19:54.340 --> 00:19:56.400
<i>What? Hey, wait!</i>

00:19:57.100 --> 00:20:01.640
Once his charge runs out, 
he'll stop moving eventually.

00:20:01.640 --> 00:20:04.970
<i>But the city will be destroyed before then!</i>

00:20:05.420 --> 00:20:10.730
<i>Oh, right. I believe that bolt 
on his head could be moved.</i>

00:20:11.160 --> 00:20:15.640
<i>You might be able to turn him off.</i>

00:20:15.900 --> 00:20:17.470
<i>Good luck.</i>

00:20:18.240 --> 00:20:19.690
She hung up.

00:20:19.690 --> 00:20:21.560
She's so irresponsible.

00:20:28.210 --> 00:20:32.250
Mai, we're aiming for the bolt 
on top of Franken's head.

00:20:32.500 --> 00:20:35.040
Got it. Leave it to me.

00:20:48.800 --> 00:20:50.280
Oh, no!

00:20:50.280 --> 00:20:51.460
It's all right.

00:20:51.460 --> 00:20:55.990
Due to how his body is constructed, he can't 
reach the top of his head with his own hands.

00:20:55.990 --> 00:20:57.360
Lucky us.

00:20:57.820 --> 00:20:59.860
Okay, let's turn this thing.

00:20:59.860 --> 00:21:02.020
Got it. I'll help you.

00:21:02.260 --> 00:21:04.100
Turn!

00:21:34.890 --> 00:21:37.350
<b>The Next Day</b>

00:21:47.990 --> 00:21:55.290
<b>Insulated</b>

00:22:03.550 --> 00:22:06.450
The snail's on the thorn;

00:22:06.450 --> 00:22:08.690
God's in His heaven,

00:22:10.260 --> 00:22:12.980
all's right with the world!

00:23:44.980 --> 00:23:59.990
<b>Episode 11 "A Midsummer Night's Operation: Mystery"</b>

00:23:45.760 --> 00:23:48.650
This remote tropical island 
is known only to a select few

00:23:48.650 --> 00:23:52.230
and completely unknown to 
those unfamiliar with it.

00:23:52.750 --> 00:23:56.130
The last paradise on earth, 
not found on any map.

00:23:56.440 --> 00:23:57.680
Unbaba Island.
